  "question": {
    "text": "$P Q$ is a double ordinate of the hyperbola $\\frac{x^2}{a^2}-\\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1$ such that $\\triangle O P Q$ is an equilateral triangle, $O$ being the centre of the hyperbola. Then the eccentricity e of the hyperbola satisfies",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "fIWPQ",
      "text": "$1  < \\mathrm{e} < 2 / \\sqrt{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "kgW9s",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{e}=2 / \\sqrt{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3BtFa",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{e}=2 \\sqrt{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dGVdP",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{e} > 2 / \\sqrt{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\tan 30^{\\circ}=\\frac{b \\tan \\theta}{a \\sec \\theta}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{1}{\\sin \\theta \\sqrt{3}}$\n$e=\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{3 \\sin ^2 \\theta}} > \\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{3}}$\n$\\Rightarrow e > \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\left(0  < \\sin ^2 \\theta < 1\\right)$<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/uqNRXOXXZnnhO2dcM-MwasaIb8EhGQUw5TVkovm_VUo.original.fullsize.png\">",
